Error [E0107]: nothing named `Secret` exists here
  --> tests/ui/crypto_hkdf_output_length.jet:6:46
    |
  6 |     safe :: crypto.hkdf_sha256(crypto.Secret.from_bytes([1]), [], [], ((8161)))
    |                                              ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: a name must be declared before it's used
 Fix: declare it first: `Secret :: ...`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0107

Error [E2402]: `?` can't convert `CryptoError` into `Err` — no declared conversion exists
  --> tests/ui/crypto_hkdf_output_length.jet:6:20
    |
  6 |     safe :: crypto.hkdf_sha256(crypto.Secret.from_bytes([1]), [], [], ((8161)))
    |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `?` uses the declared conversion rail; `CryptoError` can reach `Err` only through `impl CryptoError -> Err`
 Fix: add `impl CryptoError -> Err { … }` before this function, or change the return type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2402

